From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:58:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] vkd3d: shader model 6.6 on KosmicKrisp

KosmicKrisp has no float controls, no compute shader derivatives and no
64-bit buffer atomics (Metal has 64-bit atomic min and max only), so the
device stopped at shader model 6.0. Unreal Engine 5's Direct3D 12
renderer needs 12_0 and SM 6.6: with anything less it stops at start
with a message box (MultiVersus, En Garde!, UE 5.1.1 both).

On KosmicKrisp only: count the denorm behaviour as given (Metal has one;
a shader's requested DXIL denorm mode, optional and "any" by default, is
not honoured), and expose SM 6.6 without native compute derivatives,
as vkd3d-proton already does on pre-Turing NVIDIA, and without 64-bit
buffer atomics. A shader that uses a missing feature fails to compile;
the others run, and both games render on it. The missing features are
logged at warn level when SM 6.6 is enabled.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-30-d3d12-feature-level-12.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 libs/vkd3d/device.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/device.c b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
index f8e0fdb..3551e94 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -9766,6 +9766,12 @@ static void d3d12_device_caps_init_shader_model(struct d3d12_device *device)
             }
         }
 
+        /* KosmicKrisp: Metal has one denorm behaviour and no float controls. A shader's
+         * requested DXIL denorm mode (optional since SM 6.2, "any" by default) is not
+         * honoured there; the rest of SM 6.2 and later does not need it. */
+        if (device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_properties.driverID == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_KOSMICKRISP)
+            denorm_behavior = true;
+
         if (denorm_behavior)
         {
             device->d3d12_caps.max_shader_model = D3D_SHADER_MODEL_6_2;
@@ -9819,16 +9825,24 @@ static void d3d12_device_caps_init_shader_model(struct d3d12_device *device)
          *   If minSize == maxSize, we are trivially guaranteed the desired wave size anyways.
          * - RayPayload attribute (purely metadata in DXIL land, irrelevant for us).
          */
+        /* KosmicKrisp has neither compute shader derivatives nor 64-bit buffer atomics
+         * (Metal has 64-bit atomic min and max only), and Unreal Engine 5's Direct3D 12
+         * renderer asks for SM 6.6. Expose it there as on pre-Turing NVIDIA: a shader
+         * that uses either feature fails to compile, the rest run. */
         if (device->d3d12_caps.max_shader_model == D3D_SHADER_MODEL_6_5 &&
                 (device->device_info.compute_shader_derivatives_features_khr.computeDerivativeGroupLinear ||
-                        device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_properties.driverID == VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY) &&
-                device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_features.shaderBufferInt64Atomics &&
+                        device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_properties.driverID == VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY ||
+                        device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_properties.driverID == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_KOSMICKRISP) &&
+                (device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_features.shaderBufferInt64Atomics ||
+                        device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_properties.driverID == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_KOSMICKRISP) &&
                 device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_features.shaderInt8 &&
                 d3d12_device_supports_required_subgroup_size_for_stage(device, VK_SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE_BIT))
         {
             INFO("Enabling support for SM 6.6.\n");
             if (!device->device_info.compute_shader_derivatives_features_khr.computeDerivativeGroupLinear)
-                WARN("Enabling SM 6.6 on pre-Turing NVIDIA despite lack of native compute shader derivatives.\n");
+                WARN("Enabling SM 6.6 despite lack of native compute shader derivatives.\n");
+            if (!device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_features.shaderBufferInt64Atomics)
+                WARN("Enabling SM 6.6 despite lack of 64-bit buffer atomics.\n");
             device->d3d12_caps.max_shader_model = D3D_SHADER_MODEL_6_6;
         }
 
